That's what I /thought/ when I kept sacrificing to get Frosty, but in
reality that's not the case.  Your average Gehennom level has a mix of
"soulful" monsters and demons. The latter aren't a big threat, except
for nalfeshnees and perhaps the ones that can summon.  The former
includes things like minotaurs and q:s.

Stormy is weak when:
- you need to take out a demon quickly (Juiblex, Orcus, nalfeshnees
  and the lairless Princes)
- you're surrounded by the undead (VoTD, Orcus town)
- you still haven't genocided Liches

That IMHO leaves Stormy as a good weapon in most of Gehennom,
including the Sanctum.  Combine with an enchanted silver saber, and
you've got what you need for melee.

